<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Color Fingerprint of Czech Advertising</title>
<style>{{ inline_css }}</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>

<header>
    <h1>Color Fingerprint of Czech Advertising</h1>
    <p class="lede">Ten publicly available spots, sampled at one frame per second, clustered in CIE-LAB.</p>
    <p class="byline">{{ author }} · <a href="{{ repo_url }}">source on GitHub</a></p>
</header>

<section class="method">
<strong>Method</strong> — frames sampled at 1 fps from public YouTube uploads. Per-frame palettes via K-means (k = 5) in canonical CIE-LAB color space, where Euclidean distance approximates perceptual difference. Brand-level metrics aggregate across all retained frames of each spot.
</section>

<section>
<h2>Per-brand color strips</h2>
{% for row in brand_rows %}
<div class="brand-row">
    <div class="brand-meta">
        <p class="name">
            <span class="swatch" style="background: {{ row.anchor_hex }};"></span>{{ row.brand }}
        </p>
        <p class="sector">{{ row.sector }} · {{ row.n_frames }} frames · arc {{ row.arc_glyph }} {{ row.arc_shape }}</p>
    </div>
    {{ row.strip_html | safe }}
</div>
{% endfor %}
</section>

<section>
<h2>Cross-brand map: palette diversity vs saturation tension</h2>
{{ scatter_svg | safe }}
<p class="caption">Quadrants are split at the corpus median. Dot color = each brand's anchor swatch.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>Brand color vs on-screen color</h2>
<p class="lede-small">Distance (in degrees on the hue wheel) between the brand's anchor color and the dominant chromatic color actually on screen.</p>
{{ gap_svg | safe }}
</section>

<section>
<h2>Patterns</h2>
{% for p in patterns %}
<div class="pattern">
    <h3>{{ p.title }}</h3>
    <p class="evidence">{{ p.evidence }}</p>
    <p class="takeaway"><strong>Why it matters.</strong> {{ p.takeaway }}</p>
</div>
{% endfor %}
</section>

<section>
<h2>What this means</h2>
{% for line in conclusion %}
<p class="conclusion">{{ line }}</p>
{% endfor %}
</section>

<footer>
<p>Analysis of publicly available video material. Brands and campaigns are referenced for analytical purposes only. No agency attribution is implied.</p>
<p>Code MIT · derived data CC-BY-4.0 · source video material is not redistributed.</p>
</footer>

</main>
</body>
</html>
